## Context

Three classes of documents (author decision, 2026-09-25):

- **frozen** (signed agreements, RRPs, reports): collected once, then only
  verified (existence, link check of [[0925]], change);
- **living** (ADB project fact sheet, portfolio.jetp.id, the Vietnamese
  ministry dashboard): recollected at the frequency declared by their site
  file; each version is kept under its fingerprint, which makes a dated series
  — the ADB 56140-001 fact sheet gives, per instrument, dated cumulative
  commitments and disbursements;
- **series** (annual and quarterly reports, progress reports): each published
  issue is frozen; the series has an expected date for its next issue.

A watch module exists: `scripts/jetp/_source_watch.py`,
`scripts/jetp/build_source_sweep.py` (`new_candidate`, `changed`,
`checked_no_change`); it never admits evidence itself. Monitoring plugs into
it, it does not duplicate it.

## Actions

1. Passes run on padme. Doudou supervises: it launches, checks the report, and
   when SSH does not answer it defers the pass and says so.
2. A new link matching a site pattern, or a published series issue, becomes a
   candidate to examine, never a source admitted automatically. A figure read
   from a fact sheet remains a snapshot until it is turned into an observation
   by the usual route.
3. Each pass writes a report that flags without blocking: witness document not
   found, series issue overdue, change in robots.txt or terms of use, rung
   failure. `/lair` and `/healthcheck` surface it.
4. Objects are captured by DVC on padme at each pass that adds some. Every write
   of a document or a new version goes through a single deposit function (bytes,
   fingerprint, collection metadata), called by all passes. Milestone M4
   ([[1510]]) will replace what sits behind it (Zotero group library) without
   touching the passes; do not write to `data/jetp/documents/objects/` or to
   `snapshots.csv` anywhere but in this function.
5. The launcher builds on that of [[1141]] (persistent checkout, cron, refusal
   to overwrite an unreviewed result) and generalises it; verification of frozen
   documents is the pass of [[1141]], not a second one. Discovery beyond known
   sites is the pass of [[1140]]; its candidates enter the same queue.

## Cases carried over from the deleted backend design (ticket 1701)

Acceptance tests for source management (section 10 of the 2026-09-14
document): a blocked check records the attempt without advancing the last
successful coverage; a complete check with no change advances the schedule
without creating an observation; each target of a frozen pass has a result or an
explicit deferral; a repeated discovery keeps a single document identity; a
revision of publisher, cadence or ranking leaves unchanged an old pass and a
query dated to an earlier knowledge date; a copied report creates neither an
independent confirmation nor a duplicate payment.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An ADB fact sheet is recollected by two dated passes; a new version produces a new snapshot, an unchanged version produces none
- [ ] A real series is tracked: its next expected issue is dated, and a delay is flagged
- [ ] With SSH down, supervision from doudou defers the pass and says so; no pass disappears silently
- [ ] The flags of a pass report appear in `/lair`
- [ ] No pass writes an object or a `snapshots.csv` row outside the single deposit function (action 4)
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` green
